"Etiam quis nunc at ligula tincidunt eleifend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:0
msgid "Syntax"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:22
msgid ""
":::{aside}\n"
"An aside floats beside the flow, and the surrounding text wraps around it.\n"
":::\n"
"\n"
":::{aside} Aside title\n"
":align: left\n"
"\n"
"Asides are handy for pull-outs, margin notes and side comments.\n"
":::\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:25
msgid ""
".. aside::\n"
"\n"
"   An aside floats beside the flow, and the surrounding text wraps around "
"it.\n"
"\n"
".. aside:: Aside title\n"
"   :align: left\n"
"\n"
"   Asides are handy for pull-outs, margin notes and side comments.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:32
msgid ""
"Asides *complement* [admonitions](https://myst-parser.readthedocs.io/en/"
"latest/syntax/admonitions.html) and [cards](./cards.md): use an "
"**admonition** for a note that interrupts the flow as a full-width block, a "
"**card** for a self-contained boxed unit inside a [grid](./grids.md), and an "
"**aside** when you want the body text to keep flowing *around* a side box."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:39
msgid "Alignment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:41
msgid ""
"Use the `align` option to float the box `left` or `right` (the default is "
"`right`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:0
msgid "Floated left"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:48
msgid ""
"`:align: left` floats the box to the left, with the text wrapping down its "
"right-hand side."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:54
msgid "Widths"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:56
msgid ""
"The `width` option accepts `25%`, `33%` (the default) or `50%`, controlling "
"how much horizontal space the box occupies (and therefore how much room is "
"left for the wrapping text)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:0
msgid "A 50% aside"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:64
msgid "At `:width: 50%` the box takes up half the content width."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:72
msgid ""
"Widths are only applied from the `md` breakpoint (768&nbsp;px) upwards. "
"Below that the aside becomes a full-width block regardless of the `width` "
"option, so it stays readable on small screens. On themes with a right-hand "
"in-page table of contents (such as pydata-sphinx-theme), the main column is "
"already narrower, so a right-floated aside leaves less room for the wrapped "
"text; prefer a smaller `width` or `:align: left` there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:80
msgid "Stopping the wrap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:82
msgid ""
"Text keeps wrapping around an aside until it runs out. To force following "
"content to start *below* the box instead, add the `sd-clear-both` utility "
"class to it, for example with an empty `div` directive:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:0
msgid "Short aside"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:90
msgid "A short aside."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:97
msgid ""
"This paragraph is pushed below the aside because the preceding empty `div` "
"has the `sd-clear-both` class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:100
msgid ""
"Always clear a *trailing* aside A float is not contained by its parent "
"section, so an aside that is the **last element of a section** (with no text "
"left to wrap) can extend past the end of the section and overlap whatever "
"follows — the next heading, or content injected by the theme. When an aside "
"is the final piece of a section, follow it with a cleared block:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:107
msgid ""
".. aside:: Wrap-up note\n"
"   :align: right\n"
"\n"
"   The last content in this section.\n"
"\n"
".. div:: sd-clear-both\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:116
msgid ""
"Themes can address this globally instead, by clearfixing their main content "
"column (for example `.article-container { display: flow-root }`), which "
"contains every float without an explicit clearing element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:121
msgid "Semantic output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:123
msgid ""
"In HTML an aside is rendered as a native [`<aside>`](https://"
"developer.mozilla.org/en/docs/Web/HTML/Element/aside) element (not a plain "
"`<div>`), which correctly conveys \"tangentially related content\" to "
"assistive technologies and reader modes. In non-HTML outputs (LaTeX, "
"text, ...) it degrades to a plain titled block. No JavaScript is involved: "
"the float and the responsive collapse are pure CSS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:130
msgid ""
"A **titled** aside is labelled by its title: the `<aside>` carries an `aria-"
"labelledby` attribute pointing at the title element (which is given a "
"stable, automatically generated id when you do not supply a `:name:`), so "
"screen readers announce the region by its heading. An **untitled** aside has "
"no heading text to label it with and is intentionally left unlabelled — give "
"it a title if you want it announced as a named region."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:137
msgid "Cross-referencing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:139
msgid ""
"When you give an aside a `:name:`, the target (and therefore the `id` "
"anchor) lands on the **title** element for a titled aside, or on the "
"`<aside>` itself for an untitled one. For a titled aside `` :ref:`the-name` "
"`` renders using the title text, exactly like referencing a section:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:144
msgid ""
".. aside:: Design rationale\n"
"   :name: rationale\n"
"\n"
"   ...\n"
"\n"
"See the :ref:`rationale` aside.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:153
msgid ""
"An **untitled** named aside has no caption text, so — as with any "
"captionless target in Sphinx — a bare `` :ref:`the-name` `` cannot derive "
"its link text: it warns and renders as plain text without a link. Reference "
"it with **explicit text** instead: `` :ref:`jump to the note <the-name>` ``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:158
msgid "`aside` options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:160
msgid "align"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:161
msgid "Float direction of the aside: `left` or `right` (default `right`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:163
msgid "width"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:164
msgid ""
"Width of the aside from the `md` breakpoint up: `25%`, `33%` or `50%` "
"(default `33%`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:167
msgid "margin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:168
msgid ""
"Outer margin of the aside. One (all) or four (top bottom left right) values "
"from: 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, auto."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:171
msgid "name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:172
msgid ""
"Set a reference-able name for the aside (attached to the title, where "
"present, so it can be used as the cross-reference text)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:175
msgid "class"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:176
msgid "Additional CSS classes for the (outer) `<aside>` element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:178
msgid "class-title"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:179
msgid "Additional CSS classes for the title element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:181
msgid "class-body"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:182
msgid "Additional CSS classes for the body element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:187
msgid ""
":::{aside} Narrow, right-aligned\n"
":name: target\n"
":align: right\n"
":width: 25%\n"
":margin: 1\n"
":class: class-aside\n"
":class-title: class-title\n"
":class-body: class-body\n"
"\n"
"A 25% wide aside, floated right.\n"
":::\n"
"\n"
":::{aside} Wide, left-aligned\n"
":align: left\n"
":width: 50%\n"
"\n"
"A 50% wide aside, floated left.\n"
":::\n"
"\n"
"{ref}`target`, {ref}`text <target>`\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../asides.md:190
msgid ""
".. aside:: Narrow, right-aligned\n"
"   :name: target\n"
"   :align: right\n"
"   :width: 25%\n"
"   :margin: 1\n"
"   :class: class-aside\n"
"   :class-title: class-title\n"
"   :class-body: class-body\n"
"\n"
"   A 25% wide aside, floated right.\n"
"\n"
".. aside:: Wide, left-aligned\n"
"   :align: left\n"
"   :width: 50%\n"
"\n"
"   A 50% wide aside, floated left.\n"
"\n"
":ref:`target`, :ref:`text <target>`\n"
msgstr ""
